- Text arguments must be strings. Non-string throws `TypeError` whose message starts with the function name and a colon. Out-of-range numeric args throw `RangeError` with the same prefix. Tests assert error class and message prefix, never full message text.
- No state: no argument mutation, no caching, no environment reads. Same args → equal values.
